# JVP_MAKE_FLAGS

## Purpose

`JVP_MAKE_FLAGS` is a macro used to combine a JV kind identifier and a set of property flags into a single packed value. It ensures that only the bits belonging to each component are preserved by masking them with the appropriate bit masks (`KIND_MASK` and `PFLAGS_MASK`) before applying a bitwise OR. This produces a compact representation that can be stored and later inspected to recover both the kind and the flags.

## Signature

```c
#define JVP_MAKE_FLAGS(kind, pflags) ((kind & KIND_MASK) | (pflags & PFLAGS_MASK))
```

## Parameters

- **`kind`**  
  The JV kind value to encode. This is typically an enumeration value identifying the type of a `jv` value (e.g., null, boolean, number, string, array, object). The macro masks this value with `KIND_MASK` to retain only the bits relevant to the kind.

- **`pflags`**  
  Property flags associated with the value. These are bit flags that encode additional properties or state. The macro masks this value with `PFLAGS_MASK` to retain only the bits relevant to the flags.

## Returns

An integer value representing the combined and masked bitwise OR of `kind` and `pflags`. The result is a single packed value that can later be decomposed using complementary masks to recover the original kind and flags.

## Example Usage

```c
#include "jv.h"

/* Assume the following values are defined in the JV header */
#define JV_KIND_NULL 0
#define JV_KIND_TRUE 1
/* Assume a flag indicating an immutable value */
#define JVP_FLAG_IMMUTABLE 0x10

/* Combine a kind with a flag */
int flags = JVP_MAKE_FLAGS(JV_KIND_TRUE, JVP_FLAG_IMMUTABLE);

/* Later, the components can be recovered with the masks */
int kind = flags & KIND_MASK;
int pflags = flags & PFLAGS_MASK;

/* Verify the kind is still JV_KIND_TRUE */
assert(kind == JV_KIND_TRUE);
```

